/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (A lexical environment is basically the scope or environment the engine is currently reading code in. A new lexical environment is created when curly brackets {} are used, even nested brackets {{...}} create a new lexical environment. The execuBon context tells the engine which lexical environment it is currently working in and the lexical scope determines the available variables. )
/E (A lexical environment is basically the scope or environment the engine is currently reading code in. A new lexical environment is created when curly brackets {} are used, even nested brackets {{...}} create a new lexical environment. The execuBon context tells the engine which lexical environment it is currently working in and the lexical scope determines the available variables. )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [3]
>>
