/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Strict equals: The triple equals \(===\) or strict equality compares two values without type coercion. If the values are not the same type, then the values are not equal. This is almost always the right way to check for equality in JavaScript, so you don't accidentally coerce a value and end up with a bug in your program. Here is the MDN Equality Comparison page and the ECMAScript Comparison Algorithm. )
/E (Strict equals: The triple equals \(===\) or strict equality compares two values without type coercion. If the values are not the same type, then the values are not equal. This is almost always the right way to check for equality in JavaScript, so you don't accidentally coerce a value and end up with a bug in your program. Here is the MDN Equality Comparison page and the ECMAScript Comparison Algorithm. )
/Pg 52 0 R
/K [5]
