/T (Prototypal Inheritance  Almost all objects in Javascript pass down properBes through a prototype chain. We call this chain, prototypal inheritance. The child of the object "inherits" properBes from its parent. All objects in JavaScript are descended from the Object constructor unless deliberately created or altered to not do so. The objects inherit methods and properBes from Object.prototype. The prototype property also has an accessor property called __proto__ that creates a link between the current object and points to the object it was created from, the "prototype". )
/E (Prototypal Inheritance  Almost all objects in Javascript pass down properBes through a prototype chain. We call this chain, prototypal inheritance. The child of the object "inherits" properBes from its parent. All objects in JavaScript are descended from the Object constructor unless deliberately created or altered to not do so. The objects inherit methods and properBes from Object.prototype. The prototype property also has an accessor property called __proto__ that creates a link between the current object and points to the object it was created from, the "prototype". )
/Pg 55 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
