<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Constructor FuncAons  Using Object.create is true prototypal inheritance, the code is cleaner and easier to read. However, you will not see this being used in most programs. Before Object.create came around, we had the ability to use constructor funcBons. Constructor funcBons are exactly like the funcBon constructor we talked about above. The number and string funcBons were constructed and invoked with the new keyword and they were capitalized. The new keyword actually changes the meaning of this for the constructor )
/E (Constructor FuncAons  Using Object.create is true prototypal inheritance, the code is cleaner and easier to read. However, you will not see this being used in most programs. Before Object.create came around, we had the ability to use constructor funcBons. Constructor funcBons are exactly like the funcBon constructor we talked about above. The number and string funcBons were constructed and invoked with the new keyword and they were capitalized. The new keyword actually changes the meaning of this for the constructor )
/Pg 68 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
