/T (funcBon. Without new, this will point to the window object instead of the object that we just created. It is best pracBce to capitalize constructor funcBons to help us idenBfy them and know to use the new keyword. ProperBes added to a constructor funcBon can only be done using the this keyword, regular variables do not get added to the object. )
/E (funcBon. Without new, this will point to the window object instead of the object that we just created. It is best pracBce to capitalize constructor funcBons to help us idenBfy them and know to use the new keyword. ProperBes added to a constructor funcBon can only be done using the this keyword, regular variables do not get added to the object. )
/Pg 69 0 R
/K [1]
>>
