/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Originally in JavaScript, we had the module paUern. Before block scope came around, there was only global scope and funcBon scope. To create this idea of modules, a module scope was implemented just above the funcBon scope. This allowed variables to be shared, by exporBng and imporBng, between the funcBons without having to go through the global scope. A funcBon as a module is essenBally just an immediately invoked funcBon expression, IIFE. )
/E (Originally in JavaScript, we had the module paUern. Before block scope came around, there was only global scope and funcBon scope. To create this idea of modules, a module scope was implemented just above the funcBon scope. This allowed variables to be shared, by exporBng and imporBng, between the funcBons without having to go through the global scope. A funcBon as a module is essenBally just an immediately invoked funcBon expression, IIFE. )
/Pg 82 0 R
/K [2]
>>
